#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md:6
msgid "Defining Macros By Example"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md:8
msgid ""
"A declarative macro consists of one or more **macro rules**, similar to how "
"a Rust `match` expression consists of a sequence of match arms:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md:14
msgid "// Left-side: Matcher        Right-side: Transcriber\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md:16
msgid "\"{}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md:20
msgid ""
"**Macro Rule:** An arm of the macro containing a Matcher and a Transcriber "
"separated by `=>`."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md:22
msgid "**Matcher:** A pattern that matches an input token stream."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md:23
msgid "**Transcriber:** The code segment template that expands when matched."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md:24
msgid ""
"**Meta-variables:** Variables defined on the left and expanded on the right, "
"prefixed with `$` (e.g., `$bar`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md:26
msgid ""
"**Fragment Specifiers:** Indicate to which syntactic category the meta-"
"variable is restricted (e.g., `ident` or `expr`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md:32
msgid ""
"Like `match` in normal Rust, the compiler attempts to match each rule "
"sequentially, from top to bottom."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md:34
msgid ""
"If a rule matches the input token stream completely, it selects that arm and "
"transcribes the output."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/defining.md:36
msgid ""
"If no arms match, or if any pattern is ambiguous when matching tokens (there "
"is no backtrack or lookahead), the compiler emits an error."
msgstr ""
